$ wk init --store repo --preset general
Created <DIR>/.work (preset: general)
Skills: .claude/skills/wk, .claude/skills/wk-setup
Added the wk pointer to AGENTS.md
Next: wk brief, then the wk-setup skill (wk guide setup).
$ wk area new ui "Screens, layout\nand styling"
Area ui: Screens, layout
$ wk area new ui "again"
! Area ui already exists.
[exit 1]
$ wk area new "Bad Name" "x"
! Area names are lowercase letters, digits and dashes, like ui or front-end.
[exit 1]
$ wk area new docs
! Describe the area in a line: wk area new docs "<what it covers>"
[exit 1]
$ wk area
core       0 open tasks, 0 principles  Always in scope. Its principles load for every task; items with no better home live here.
ui         0 open tasks, 0 principles  Screens, layout
$ wk decide "Use plain files"
! A decision needs a reason: --why "<why>"
[exit 1]
$ wk decide "Use plain files" --why "Diffs stay readable\nNo server" --rejected "A database"
Decision 4yrm Use plain files (core)
$ wk learn "Git stores CRLF on Windows\nset autocrlf"
Learning aes8 Git stores CRLF on Windows (core)
$ wk learn "1\n2\n3"
! Learning is 3 lines, limit is 2 (1 over). Shorten it.
[exit 1]
$ wk principle "Keep commands short"
! Name the default it overrides: --instead "<what a model would do otherwise>". If there is none, it isn't a principle.
[exit 1]
$ wk principle "Keep commands short" --instead "long flags"
! Say why: --because "<reason>"
[exit 1]
$ wk principle "Keep commands short" --instead "long flags" --because "agents type them\nmany times" --in ui --test "lint:flags"
Principle yebg Keep commands short (ui)
$ wk principle "Keep all commands short" --instead "x" --because "y" --in ui
! Similar: yebg Keep commands short
! Edit or supersede it instead.
[exit 1]
$ wk principle "Prefer files" --instead "databases" --because "diffs" --from 4yrm
Principle xcma Prefer files (core)
$ wk principle "Prefer text" --instead "binary" --because "diffs" --from aes8
Principle m7sw Prefer text (core)
$ wk principle "Old rule" --instead "a" --because "b" --in ui
Principle xr8y Old rule (ui)
$ wk supersede 4yrm aes8
! 4yrm is a decision; aes8 is a learning.
[exit 1]
$ wk area list
core       0 open tasks, 2 principles  Always in scope. Its principles load for every task; items with no better home live here.
ui         0 open tasks, 2 principles  Screens, layout
$ wk show aes8
aes8  learning · core
Git stores CRLF on Windows
distilled_into: m7sw
created 2026-11-10 · updated 2026-11-10

set autocrlf
$ wk add "Polish the header"
Added xewh Polish the header (core)
$ wk add "Header polish pass" --force --tags ux
Added vn5c Header polish pass (core)
New tag: ux (known: quick).
$ wk add "Fix the footer"
Added rrfd Fix the footer (core)
$ wk edit 4yrm --title "Nope"
! Decisions are never edited. Record a new one and run: wk supersede <old> <new>
[exit 1]
$ wk edit xcma
! Nothing to change. Use --title, --body, --tags, --instead, --because or --ref.
[exit 1]
$ wk edit xcma --title "Fix the sticky footer" --tags bug,ux --ref T-12 --body "Seen on mobile"
Updated xcma Fix the sticky footer
$ wk edit xcma --instead "nothing"
Updated xcma Fix the sticky footer
$ wk merge 4yrm 4yrm
! Can't merge an item into itself.
[exit 1]
$ wk ls
queue   xewh Polish the header (core)
queue   vn5c Header polish pass (core) #ux
queue   rrfd Fix the footer (core)
$ wk drop 4yrm
! decisions are superseded, not dropped: wk supersede <old> <new>
[exit 1]
